<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
The privacy manifest of Deckie, the iPad app. No tracking, no tracking domains, no data collected: the microphone's sound is
heard on the iPad and never leaves it, and there is no account.

The APIs Apple asks a reason for, as the app uses them (checked in deck-app/Deck/Sources and the core targets the app
links, DeckieCore, DeckieCrate, DeckieRecognition and DeckieAudio):
- UserDefaults (CA92.1, the app's own settings): the crate file open, Minimal, the Shuffle dial, the recogniser
  chosen, the Crate tab's Details switch.
- File timestamps (C617.1, files inside the app's container): the modification date of Deckie's index beside the
  crate file in Application Support, to tell whether it was made just now or reused (for the log). Reading a
  cover checks its size and type the same way.
- System boot time (35F9.1, time between events in the app): DispatchTime's uptime clock, to time how long one
  reading of the recogniser takes.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>35F9.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
